## Id namespaces

`nav.main.*` · `dashboard.{stats,recent,chart}.*` · `transactions.{add,filters,list,table,summary,delete-dialog}.*` + `transaction.form.*` · `categories.{add,income,expense,delete-dialog}.*` + `category.form.*` · `reports.{month,summary,chart.daily,income-by-category,expenses-by-category}.*` · `tax.{year,print,summary,income-by-category,expenses-by-category,transactions}.*` · `not-found.*`

The singular/plural split (`transaction.form.*` vs `transactions.*`) keeps modal forms from colliding with the list page behind them when both are mounted.

## Collections (14, all folding)

`nav.main`, `dashboard.stats`, `dashboard.recent`, `transactions.table`, `categories.income`, `categories.expense`, `category.form.colors`, `reports.summary`, `reports.income-by-category`, `reports.expenses-by-category`, `tax.summary`, `tax.income-by-category`, `tax.expenses-by-category`, `tax.transactions`.

All keyed on stable domain ids (`tx-N`, `cat-N`) or semantic slugs — never array index.

## Not folded, by design

- **Select option lists** use the spec's `.option.<value>` shape rather than `.item.`, because Radix portals `SelectContent` outside the trigger's subtree and only mounts it while open. `data-semtag-options` on each trigger is the spec's substitute.
- **`tax.*-by-category.total` rows** sit inside collection tables but deliberately are not `.item.` ids — they're totals, not members, and folding them would misrepresent the row count.

## Deliberately unhinted

Recharts internals (SVG geometry, legends, tooltips — only the containers carry `region`); decorative icons and colour badges that restate an adjacent labelled control; layout wrappers (`MainLayout`, `App.tsx` routing); page headings and static `<th>` labels; print-only blocks in TaxSummary; and the whole `src/components/ui/*` shadcn library — untouched, since every component there already spreads `...props`, so hints pass through from call sites.

## Notable correctness work

- **`StatCard`** got the one permitted prop-widening (three optional `data-semtag-*` props forwarded to the value `<p>`, not the card root — the root's text would concatenate title + value + subtitle + trend). Attributes are emitted only when the id is present, per §8.
- **`CategoryCard`** takes a `collectionId` prop, because the same component renders in both the income and expense grids; without it, a category appearing in both would emit duplicate ids.
- **`TaxSummary`** originally keyed on `category?.id`. The app allows deleting a category while its transactions survive, so two orphaned rows would both emit `…item.undefined`. I exposed the raw `categoryId` from the `summary` memo and keyed all six ids on it. The linter cannot see this — it needed reading the delete flow.

